{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":218992,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-01-06T23:36:27.199Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eBack in 2022, \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dstufft\"\u003e@dstufft\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-694-upload-2-0-api-for-python-package-repositories/16879\"\u003estarted a conversation\u003c/a\u003e about PEP 694, proposing a PyPI Upload 2.0 API.  That discussion petered out back in October, but as it’s something I’m keenly interested in, I am restarting the discussion here in a new thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI just \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/3997\"\u003emerged a significant update\u003c/a\u003e to \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/\"\u003ePEP 694\u003c/a\u003e, also making myself co-author.  I think that, and the 70+ messages in the other thread are enough to warrant a new discussion thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile the spirit and definition of the API proposed in the previous incarnation of the PEP is largely retained, some highlights of the changes I made\u003csup class=\"footnote-ref\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#footnote-218992-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-218992-1\"\u003e[1]\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdded myself as a co-author.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChanged some terminology to use “stage” rather than “draft” to describe the thing you are uploading non-public wheels to in a session.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProposed the root URL for PyPI to be \u003ccode\u003ehttps://upload.pypi.org/2.0\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdded an optional “nonce” string to the session creation request, which allows clients to decide whether a staged preview is easily guessable or not.  Both use cases, as well as the justification for “guessability” rather than “privacy” are \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-token\"\u003edescribed in more detail in the PEP\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRenamed many of the JSON keys to better align with the change in terminology.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdded or modified APIs for getting the \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-status\"\u003esession status\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-extension\"\u003eextending a session\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-cancellation\"\u003ecanceling a session\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-completion\"\u003epublishing a session\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdated the file upload protocol to better align with the \u003ca href=\"https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-httpbis-resumable-upload-05.html\"\u003eactive internet draft\u003c/a\u003e as the successor to the older \u003ca href=\"https://tus.io/\"\u003etus.io\u003c/a\u003e protocol.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSeveral other smaller changes which hopefully fill any gaps in the previous protocol.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRather than post the full text of the updated PEP 694 here, please head on over to the \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/\"\u003epublished version\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheers!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr class=\"footnotes-sep\"\u003e\n\n\u003col class=\"footnotes-list\"\u003e\n\u003cli id=\"footnote-218992-1\" class=\"footnote-item\"\u003e\u003cp\u003ebesides copyediting and formatting \u003ca href=\"#footnote-ref-218992-1\" class=\"footnote-backref\"\u003e↩︎\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-01-06T23:36:27.199Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":175,"reads":139,"readers_count":138,"score":1032.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":23},{"url":"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/3997","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694: Updates by warsaw · Pull Request #3997 · python/peps · GitHub","clicks":6},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-694-upload-2-0-api-for-python-package-repositories/16879","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694: Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Repositories","clicks":6},{"url":"https://tus.io/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"tus - resumable file uploads","clicks":3},{"url":"https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-httpbis-resumable-upload-05.html","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Resumable Uploads for HTTP","clicks":3},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-token","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":1},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-completion","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-extension","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-cancellation","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#session-status","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0-round-3/107923","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP 694 -- PyPI upload API 2.0 (Round 3)","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0-round-2/101483","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP 694 -- PyPI upload API 2.0 (Round 2)","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":9}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":17,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":9}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":9,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":236229,"name":"Michał Górny","username":"mgorny","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/{size}/34029_2.png","created_at":"2025-03-25T06:15:46.185Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eOverall, it is very solid and I like it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA few minor points:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the upload completes successfully, the server \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e respond with a \u003ccode\u003e201 Created\u003c/code\u003e status.\u003cbr\u003e\n[…]\u003cbr\u003e\nFor each successful chunk, the server \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e respond with a \u003ccode\u003e202 Accepted\u003c/code\u003e header, except for the final chunk, which \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e be a \u003ccode\u003e201 Created\u003c/code\u003e, and as with non-chunked uploads, the body of these responses has no content.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis seems to assume the processing of the final chunk will always be synchronous, which is a bit inconsistent with how the session is handled asynchronously. I can imagine that at this point, there could be some delay, e.g. because server verifies the checksum of the uploaded file in one step. However, I’m not sure if making this potentially asynchronous (i.e. returning 202 and expecting the client to recheck status later) is worth the added complexity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the offset provided in \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Offset\u003c/code\u003e is not \u003ccode\u003e0\u003c/code\u003e or correctly specifies the byte offset of the next chunk in an incomplete upload, then the server \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e respond with a \u003ccode\u003e409 Conflict\u003c/code\u003e. This means that a client \u003cstrong\u003eMAY NOT\u003c/strong\u003e upload chunks out of order.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI find this sentence really hard to parse. It sounds like it means “if the offset … correctly specifies the byte offset of the next chunk in an incomplete upload, then the server…” — but wasn’t it supposed to mean the opposite of that? Also, shouldn’t that be “MUST NOT”? “MAY NOT” is not in \u003ca href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRFC 2119\u003c/a\u003e, and I honestly find it confusing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePerhaps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the offset provided in \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Offset\u003c/code\u003e is not \u003ccode\u003e0\u003c/code\u003e and does not correctly specify the byte offset of the next chunk in an incomplete upload, then the server \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e respond with a \u003ccode\u003e409 Conflict\u003c/code\u003e. This means that a client \u003cstrong\u003eMUST NOT\u003c/strong\u003e upload chunks out of order.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#canceling-an-in-progress-upload\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCanceling an In-Progress Upload\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n[…]\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#delete-a-partial-or-fully-uploaded-file\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDelete a Partial or Fully Uploaded File\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIsn’t “deleting a partial file” and “canceling an upload” essentially the same thing? Also, the latter section only covers fully uploaded files, so perhaps it should either be renamed, or both sections merged into one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#complete-the-upload\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eComplete the in-progress upload\u003c/a\u003e by uploading a zero-length chunk providing the \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?1\u003c/code\u003e header. This effectively truncates and completes the in-progress upload, after which point the new upload can commence. In this case, clients \u003cstrong\u003eSHOULD\u003c/strong\u003e reuse the previous upload resource URL and do not need to begin the entire \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#file-uploads\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003efile upload\u003c/a\u003e sequence over again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat is the use case for this? FWIU it implies that the file must have the same size and hashes, so I don’t really understand what would be the circumstances under which the client would suddenly need to start uploading the same file over again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think error responses are underspecified. In particular, HTTP error codes are listed only in handful of cases. I think it would be worthwhile to at least list some common errors that can be expected from issuing different requests.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-03-25T06:16:30.528Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":14,"reads":92,"readers_count":91,"score":93.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Michał Górny","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#file-uploads","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":1},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#complete-the-upload","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"RFC 2119: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels","clicks":0},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#delete-a-partial-or-fully-uploaded-file","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#canceling-an-in-progress-upload","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":6712,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":236397,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-03-25T20:45:21.481Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOverall, it is very solid and I like it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks for the vote of confidence!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis seems to assume the processing of the final chunk will always be synchronous, which is a bit inconsistent with how the session is handled asynchronously.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think I took this from the IETF draft, but at this point, PEP 694 uses that more as inspiration rather than a faithful implementation\u003csup class=\"footnote-ref\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#footnote-236397-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-236397-1\"\u003e[1]\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think you have a point; both that the API for the final chunk probably should allow for either a \u003ccode\u003e201\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003e202\u003c/code\u003e response here.  I think we could relax this to accept either code.  If a \u003ccode\u003e202\u003c/code\u003e is returned, the client would have to do a \u003ccode\u003eHEAD\u003c/code\u003e request as per \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#resume-an-upload\"\u003eresume an upload\u003c/a\u003e, and the server would response with the \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Offset\u003c/code\u003e indicating the full file has been received, along with an \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?0\u003c/code\u003e header.  The client would continue to do \u003ccode\u003eHEAD\u003c/code\u003e requests until they see a response with \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?1\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWDYT?  If this is workable, it doesn’t seem like a huge additional complication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr class=\"footnotes-sep\"\u003e\n\n\u003col class=\"footnotes-list\"\u003e\n\u003cli id=\"footnote-236397-1\" class=\"footnote-item\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eplus, the draft expires on 24 April 2025 and I see no status updates to it \u003ca href=\"#footnote-ref-236397-1\" class=\"footnote-backref\"\u003e↩︎\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-03-25T20:45:21.481Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":76,"readers_count":75,"score":20.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/#resume-an-upload","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 694 – Upload 2.0 API for Python Package Indexes | peps.python.org","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":17,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":236400,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-03-25T21:14:07.893Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI find this sentence really hard to parse.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks for calling this out.  I think I misspelled “incorrectly” there.  Your suggestion LGTM!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIsn’t “deleting a partial file” and “canceling an upload” essentially the same thing? Also, the latter section only covers fully uploaded files, so perhaps it should either be renamed, or both sections merged into one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnother good point.  I think merging these sections is the right way to go.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat is the use case for this? FWIU it implies that the file must have the same size and hashes, so I don’t really understand what would be the circumstances under which the client would suddenly need to start uploading the same file over again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpon re-reading this, I agree.  It’s superfluous, and there should be OOWTDI.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think error responses are underspecified. In particular, HTTP error codes are listed only in handful of cases. I think it would be worthwhile to at least list some common errors that can be expected from issuing different requests.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood call.  I’ll do a pass to flesh out more of the error responses, and then post a PR to update the PEP.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks for the in-depth reading and excellent feedback!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-03-25T21:14:07.893Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":79,"readers_count":78,"score":20.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":17,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":236423,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-03-25T23:26:41.556Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"barry\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/48/42_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Barry Warsaw:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePR to update the PEP\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox githubpullrequest\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003egithub.com/python/peps\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\"\u003e\n\n\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"Pull Request\"\u003e\n      \u003csvg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M11 11.28V5c-.03-.78-.34-1.47-.94-2.06C9.46 2.35 8.78 2.03 8 2H7V0L4 3l3 3V4h1c.27.02.48.11.69.31.21.2.3.42.31.69v6.28A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 10 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72zm-1 2.92c-.66 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2zM4 3c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2a1.993 1.993 0 0 0-1 3.72v6.56A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 2 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72V4.72c.59-.34 1-.98 1-1.72zm-.8 10c0 .66-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2-.65 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2zM2 4.2C1.34 4.2.8 3.65.8 3c0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-info-container\"\u003e\n\n\n\n      \u003ch4\u003e\n        \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eSeveral updates based on Michal Gorny's feedback on DPO\u003c/a\u003e\n      \u003c/h4\u003e\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"branches\"\u003e\n      \u003ccode\u003emain\u003c/code\u003e ← \u003ccode\u003ewarsaw:pep694-updates\u003c/code\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n      \u003cdiv class=\"github-info\"\u003e\n        \u003cdiv class=\"date\"\u003e\n          opened \u003cspan class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2025-03-25\" data-time=\"23:26:05\" data-timezone=\"UTC\"\u003e11:26PM - 25 Mar 25 UTC\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"user\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/warsaw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003e\n            \u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/cf82a7e6a1364604fc26a4a877409deb180713fb.jpeg\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"606060\"\u003e\n            warsaw\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"lines\" title=\"1 commits changed 1 files with 36 additions and 36 deletions\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323/files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"added\"\u003e+36\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"removed\"\u003e-36\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\"\u003e\n    \u003cp class=\"github-body-container\"\u003ehttps://discuss.python.org/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/2\n\nSummary:\n* \u003cspan class=\"show-more-container\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"show-more\"\u003e…\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"excerpt hidden\"\u003eAdd some error return code descriptions where they were underspecified\n* Fix some misspellings and poorly worded text\n* Combine the canceling and deleting of upload files sections\n* Simplify the rules for replacing a staged but not yet published file\n* Add open question about deferring stage previews\n* Update `Post-History` header\n\n\n----\n📚 Documentation preview 📚: https://pep-previews--4323.org.readthedocs.build/\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-03-25T23:26:41.556Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":76,"readers_count":75,"score":15.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/peps/pull/4323","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Several updates based on Michal Gorny's feedback on DPO by warsaw · Pull Request #4323 · python/peps · GitHub","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":17,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":236475,"name":"Michał Górny","username":"mgorny","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/{size}/34029_2.png","created_at":"2025-03-26T05:31:04.280Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"barry\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/48/42_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Barry Warsaw:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe client would continue to do \u003ccode\u003eHEAD\u003c/code\u003e requests until they see a response with \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?1\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWell, my immediate thought is that you’d do a session status request to see the status of the file. Not saying I dislike this solution, just saying what immediately came to my mind as the “obvious” next step.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI suppose this also opens the question of whether you can start uploading the next file before processing of the current one finishes. Logically, I’d say not, but this would imply that we either need to make the status check obligatory, or the clients skipping it would quasi-randomly succeed or fail uploading the next file, depending on whether they issue the request before or after the processing happens to finish.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-03-26T05:31:04.280Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":77,"readers_count":76,"score":20.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Michał Górny","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":6712,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":237924,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-01T17:49:57.631Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWell, my immediate thought is that you’d do a session status request to see the status of the file. Not saying I dislike this solution, just saying what immediately came to my mind as the “obvious” next step.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a great perspective, thanks!  Thinking it over more, I agree.  I’m going to\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdate the spec to emphasize this procedure.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRewrite file status values to better support this use case\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExplicitly allow either a 201 or 202 response to the last chunk upload (i.e. \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?1\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI thought about whether for non-chunked uploads (which also contain the \u003ccode\u003eUpload-Complete: ?1\u003c/code\u003e header) should also allow either a 201 or 202, but for now, I’m not changing that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mgorny\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mgorny/48/34029_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Michał Górny:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI suppose this also opens the question of whether you can start uploading the next file before processing of the current one finishes. Logically, I’d say not, but this would imply that we either need to make the status check obligatory, or the clients skipping it would quasi-randomly succeed or fail uploading the next file, depending on whether they issue the request before or after the processing happens to finish.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s also a good point.  The PEP explicitly disallows parallel uploads of chunks, but is actually silent on whether multiple \u003cem\u003efiles\u003c/em\u003e can be uploaded in parallel.  The PEP needs to be explicit, but it can also waffle, leaving it to server implementations to allow parallel file uploads or not.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-04-01T17:49:57.631Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":74,"readers_count":73,"score":34.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":17,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0/76316/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":240901,"name":"Barry Warsaw","username":"barry","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-14T22:04:44.979Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"barry\" data-post=\"7\" data-topic=\"76316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/barry/48/42_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Barry Warsaw:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s also a good point. The PEP explicitly disallows parallel uploads of chunks, but is actually silent on whether multiple \u003cem\u003efiles\u003c/em\u003e can be uploaded in parallel. The PEP needs to be explicit, but it can also waffle, leaving it to server implementations to allow parallel file uploads or not.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd I’m finally getting around to updating the PEP, to read:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the server determines the upload cannot proceed, it \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e return a \u003ccode\u003e409 Conflict\u003c/code\u003e.  The server \u003cstrong\u003eMAY\u003c/strong\u003e allow parallel uploads of files, but is not required to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":10,"updated_at":"2025-04-14T22:04:44.979Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":72,"readers_count":71,"score":14.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":76316,"topic_slug":"pep-694-pypi-upload-api-2-0","display_username":"Barry Warsaw","prima